new file mode 100644
index 0000000..236464e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/gpu/apple-usb4-consolidation.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,185 @@
+Apple M1 USB4 storage and dock display consolidation
+===================================================
+
+This downstream draft combines the storage preparation of 2026-10-29
+(Test40 functional source, with Test49 diagnostics preserved separately)
+and the dock-display source validated through Test128. It does not include
+AMDGPU, TTM, Radeon audio, or FFmpeg changes. Native PCIe transport is generic
+at the device-enumeration level; that does not imply safe eGPU surprise removal.
+
+The Linux NVMe host driver and its firmware are unchanged. The storage side
+provides the Apple PCIe-C host, DART stream/lifetime handling, MSI offline
+handling, CD321x mode transitions, native-port association and topology-driven
+PCIe hotplug. Read/write and the recorded storage hotplug cases were validated
+in earlier test configurations. Retained-power suspend-to-idle is implemented in the follow-up described below;
+full controller power-loss restoration remains deferred.
+The reset ACK completion semantics are a separate unresolved diagnostic point.
+
+Configuration and topology
+--------------------------
+
+In addition to the display configuration documented in
+``apple-usb4-dpin-draft.rst``, enable::
+
+    CONFIG_PCIE_APPLE=y
+    CONFIG_PCIE_APPLE_PCIEC=y
+    CONFIG_PCI_MSI=y
+    CONFIG_HOTPLUG_PCI=y
+    CONFIG_HOTPLUG_PCI_PCIE=y
+    CONFIG_APPLE_DART=m
+    CONFIG_TYPEC_TPS6598X=m
+    CONFIG_BLK_DEV_NVME=m
+
+The new native host is a separate opt-in configuration. The J274 board DTS
+references the real NHI nodes rather than overlay-created diagnostic clones.
+It carries the tested cold-init flag, nonposted container property, coherent
+DMA contract and firmware-node port relationships. ACIO PCIe references are
+board-scoped. Do not copy runtime firmware memory addresses into this source.
+
+For the later combined boot comparison retain the measured storage policy::
+
+    pcie_apple_pciec.pciec_topology_events=1
+    pcie_apple_pciec.pciec_link_events=0
+    pcie_apple_pciec.pciec_reset_ack_clear=0
+    pciehp.pciehp_poll_mode=0
+    pci=hpbussize=16
+
+The ACK override preserves the earlier measured condition. It does not settle
+whether ACK_PENDING means request admission or completion. ACK classification
+changes remain excluded. The separate Test49 diagnostic module is not a
+production dependency.
+
+What was consolidated
+---------------------
+
+The archived storage comparison had changes already present in its initial
+working tree: the USB4 DART bitmap/enable-register correction and CD321x USB4
+role quiescing, plus the PCI dynamic-OF changeset ownership backport based on
+Herve Codina v12 10/10. All are included relative to the reconstructed pristine Ubuntu
+source package. Omitting them would silently lose part of the measured setup.
+
+The storage and display series both change thunderbolt/apple.c, tb.c and tb.h.
+The combined source retains the storage reset/prepare/unprepare and topology
+callbacks together with the display provider and ready/retirement callbacks.
+The only textual merge conflict was at the display-provider include: the native
+PCIe helper functions and that include are both retained. Display's queued
+initial replay (Test125) remains in place.
+
+A full Kconfig pass found a cycle introduced by the display packaging's optional
+dependency expressions. Those expressions were removed; IS_REACHABLE stubs
+handle absent or unreachable providers. The documented modular configuration
+uses all required providers together.
+
+Provenance and validation limits
+-------------------------------
+
+Target source is UbuntuAsahi/linux at
+f7734f4c91c0f47d9e762786968057bec99a0788. Reconstruction used the matching Ubuntu
+source package, not a complete checkout of that commit. Exported patches must
+pass the supplied preimage checks on an actual checkout before application.
+
+Vidya Sagar's MSI fix (2e2f69fc8ae2) and Ramzi Abdiche's EPIC fix retain their
+original commit authors and existing trailers. Adapted PCIe and DT work credits
+DjDeveloperr and Chris Kearney; original reference mails are archived. Display
+references and existing source copyrights remain. The local consolidation and
+adaptations are AI-assisted; no additional upstream endorsement is claimed.
+
+This is a source preparation for later hardware testing. Earlier individual
+hardware successes are evidence for the inputs, not a successful boot of this
+newly combined kernel. The review package records application, configuration,
+compilation and topology results separately. No kernel, bootloader, module or
+firmware is installed by generating or applying this patch series. Remaining
+diagnostic identifiers, binding documentation, style and submission cleanup
+are explicitly not represented as completed upstream review.
+
+Whole-dock retirement and external display audio (DP126--DP128)
+--------------------------------------------------------------
+
+DWC3 PIPE shutdown now retains the shared PHY in USB4/TBT mode. The Type-C
+SAFE transition remains responsible for the final PHY power-off after CIO
+retirement. Native USB3 power-off is unchanged.
+
+CIO closes new display leases and serializes transitions. With the CIO mutex
+released, the connection manager closes old-domain event admission, drains
+callbacks and asks DCP to withdraw HPD and release its display connection while
+CIO/PHY are still powered. Only successful firmware and provider release clear
+the state for a new connection. Child removal and the existing PCIe/DART
+unprepare follow. The storage diagnostic-cycle path takes the same transition
+lock; it does not bypass the retirement protocol.
+
+J274's external audio endpoint is enabled in the board DTS. Audio remains an
+explicit opt-in through the existing driver parameter::
+
+    appledrm.hdmi_audio=1
+
+For a modular driver the equivalent setting is::
+
+    options appledrm hdmi_audio=1
+
+Despite its name this parameter enables DCP DisplayPort audio too. It does
+not enable a Radeon/eGPU audio path and changes no global audio default. The
+runtime option must accompany the DT change in any later diagnostic boot;
+merely compiling this series does not activate audio in an installed system.
+
+DP127 passed one whole-dock physical disconnect/reconnect with returned image,
+USB-storage checksum and dock Ethernet. DP128 repeated the whole-dock cycle
+with audio enabled: the user heard the same bounded 48 kHz stereo test tone
+before and after reconnect, and confirmed the image returned. Playback was
+closed during removal. The OWC was on a USB/SSD dock port, so that checksum
+is USB-storage evidence, not a new native-NVMe test. These isolated module
+runs do not replace a hardware boot of the combined storage/display kernel.
+
+Active-playback removal, HDMI audio, suspend/resume, multi-monitor MST and
+unprepared eGPU removal remain outside this result. A pre-existing early
+IOMMU probe warning was recorded in DP128; the full journal is not claimed
+warning-free. ACK_PENDING belongs to the native PCIe-C reset and is not settled
+by successful DP/audio retirement. Its measured boot override is unchanged.
+
+Retained-power system suspend
+-----------------------------
+
+The follow-up uses the power domains already attached to each ACIO instance
+and the power domain owned by its Type-C PHY. It requires no port addresses,
+synthetic always-on domain, or user-selected diagnostic suspend mode.
+
+A genpd power-off notifier rejects power loss while ACIO is running. Startup
+errors and completed shutdown release the restriction before dropping the
+runtime-PM links. A PHY notifier applies the corresponding restriction only
+in USB4/Thunderbolt mode. The existing Type-C teardown order stops ACIO before
+switching the PHY away from that mode. The notifiers do not access MMIO or
+acquire driver mutexes under the genpd lock. All notifiers are removed before
+the managed power-domain attachments are released.
+
+The NHI uses the existing domain freeze/thaw helpers at the normal device-PM
+stage to stop control DMA before DART suspend and restart it after DART resume.
+Existing supplier links order the native PCIe consumers. The active-cable
+prepare veto is replaced with power-readiness checks for s2idle. Hibernation
+and deeper suspend with an active connection are still unsupported, because
+these require restoration after loss of controller state.
+
+Rejected power-off counters for retained domains may increase: this records
+the deliberate decision not to invoke the hardware power-off operation. No
+reset-ACK error is reclassified or suppressed. Energy consumption has not
+been measured, and this implementation does not claim minimum sleep power.
+
+Validation used matched diagnostic Test40 modules with the same new retention
+and NHI PM logic, rather than a boot of the entire consolidated kernel:
+
+* Test154: late/noirq PM rehearsal passed with normal UART and watchdog.
+* Test155: actual s2idle, power-button wake, HDMI returned; 1 GiB direct-read
+  hashes on TB3 Yottamaster NVMe and OWC USB/UAS plus 64 MiB on SD matched.
+* Test156: software ACIO shutdown/start released the PCIe domain (its power-off
+  usage counter incremented); the NVMe device re-enumerated asynchronously
+  and the same three data checks passed.
+* Test157: actual s2idle after that controller restart with normal asynchronous
+  device PM enabled; power-button wake, HDMI and all three hashes passed.
+
+The test-only Apple module retains earlier diagnostics solely for collection;
+those diagnostics and their ACK experiments are not dependencies of this
+source series. No NVMe, UART, watchdog, eGPU or shared TTM change is added.
+
+The existing DCP PMU read diagnostic is still observed with successful HDMI
+resume. Whole-kernel validation, active dock-display sleep, native USB4 NVMe,
+removal while asleep, write-after-resume, and power-loss recovery remain
+separate validation work. Tests are evidence for the measured topology, not
+proof for every supported device or connection state.
